.TH BOOTSTASHD 8 "September 2026" "bootstash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bootstashd \- convenience cubby for bootstrap files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstashd
[\fB\-V\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-defaults\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-pam\-helper\fR \fIpath\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bootstashd
is the bootstash daemon. After Google OpenID Connect and a one-time PAM
link to an existing Unix account, it serves the linked user’s tree
(read/write) over HTTP or HTTPS.
.PP
Packaged
.B TLS=auto
uses HTTPS when a cert pair exists.
.B TLS=no
keeps TCP binds on HTTP; the Let’s Encrypt hook then does not copy
.I live/
and removes dest PEMs under
.IR /etc/bootstash/certs
(see
.BR bootstash (5)).
.PP
HTTP
.B DELETE
removes a file or empty directory in a writable tree (not rename).
.PP
OpenVPN Connect URL import pastes
.B PUBLIC_URL
(the origin, not a file path) and probes
.B HEAD
or
.B GET /openvpn-api/profile .
The daemon answers
.B Ovpn-WebAuth
(\fBbootstash,external\fR) on that probe and on a
.B 401
from
.B /rest/GetUserlogin
and
.B /rest/GetAutologin
so Connect opens a normal browser instead of a password dialog.
Then the usual Google sign-in. Once linked, a browser GET of that URL
is a page that opens
.B openvpn://import-profile/
with a one-time token (60 seconds, two GETs, then 404) so Connect can fetch
.B client.ovpn
(or the only
.BR .ovpn ).
Several
.B .ovpn
files without a unique
.B client.ovpn
are a picker on that page (tap one; the app is not opened
automatically).
The imported profile’s display name is the OpenVPN
.B remote
host, then the cubby filename in brackets
(\fIremote\fP [\fIfilename\fP]).
The URL you paste is still
.BR PUBLIC_URL ;
that is not the tunnel endpoint.
Cubby GET of
.B .ovpn
is the file as stored (session cookie).
.B ?token=
is a capability URL (60 seconds).
.B OVPN_TOKEN=no
or cubby
.B .bootstash-no-ovpn-token
turns tokens off; Save plus Connect’s file picker still work.
This is not Access Server Basic Auth.
See
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/OPENVPN.md .
.PP
It is a convenience store, not a high-assurance secrets engine. Isolation
is a path jail plus POSIX permissions; the process runs as one service
user
.BR bootstash .
.PP
The daemon refuses to start until
.B PUBLIC_URL
is set or can be derived from
.B CERT_NAME
(or
.B hostname \-f
if none) and the first TCP
.B LISTEN
port, and
.B OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
is set (usually the Google client JSON in
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json ).
.PP
PAM for
.B POST /link
is a setuid helper
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/pam
(not on
.BR PATH ).
UID 0 is never linked (the helper does not check that password).
Operators do not run it. Do not set systemd
.B NoNewPrivileges= .
An operator drops that map with
.B bootstash unlink
.RB ( bootstash (8));
there is no HTTP
.BR /unlink .
Changing or disabling the Unix account does not drop the map.
The listing and link pages offer
.B Sign out
.RB ( POST /logout ):
this session cookie only; the PAM map stays.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version from
.B git describe
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-check\-config
Parse dist defaults, operator config, secrets file, LISTEN specs, and
TLS files when HTTPS is on (skipped if
.BR TLS=no ).
Print a short summary and exit. Does not listen.
.TP
.BI \-defaults " path"
Dist defaults file. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist .
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Operator config. Default:
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-secrets " path"
OIDC client secrets. Default:
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json .
.TP
.BI \-pam\-helper " path"
Setuid PAM helper. Default:
.IR /usr/lib/bootstash/pam .
Not an operator tool.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read dist defaults, operator config, and the secrets file
(keep the last good config on parse failure),
reload TLS certificate and key from disk when HTTPS is on (keep the
previous cert on failure;
.B TLS=no
does not load PEMs and recreates TCP listeners as HTTP), reapply cubby
.B 2770
and file
.BR 0640 ,
and re-sync CIDR/interface listeners without dropping unrelated
listeners. systemd
.B reload
sends this.
.TP
.B SIGTERM / SIGINT
Graceful shutdown. Under systemd the process sends
.B STOPPING=1
then closes listeners.
.PP
The packaged unit is
.B Type=notify
.RB ( READY=1
after config is loaded, including while waiting for a missing interface).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/default-dist
Dist defaults (not a conffile; packaged operator keys, not OIDC).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bootstash/pam
Setuid PAM helper
.RB ( 4750
.BR root:bootstash
after configure). The
daemon execs it for
.BR /link .
Not on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.I /etc/default/bootstash
Operator config
.RB ( 0644
.BR root:root );
commented
.BR DATA ,
.BR LISTEN ,
.BR PUBLIC_URL ,
and
.BR ADMIN_USERS
on install. See
.BR bootstash (5).
.TP
.I /etc/bootstash/oidc-google.json
Google OIDC client id/secret. Written by
.B bootstash provision-google .
Not a conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bootstash
Default data volume
.RB ( 0751 )
so a cubby owner can traverse in:
.IR users/<pam_user>/
.RB ( 2770
.IR alice:bootstash ).
Parent
.I users/
is
.B 0711
so that user can
.B bootstash put
(or copy with
.BR cp )
from a shell without listing other cubbies.
.B bootstash put
must run as the cubby owner, not root; files are
.B 0660
and new directories
.B 2770
(same as the cubby).
Ordinary
.B cp
(not
.BR "cp \-a" )
picks up group
.B bootstash
from setgid.
Do not
.B chown
to
.BR bootstash .
Start and SIGHUP reapply
.B 2770
on existing cubbies and linked names.
Each
.B /home
GET or HEAD also fixes that path and, for a listing, its
immediate children.
Regular cubby files are
.B chgrp
to
.B bootstash
with
.B g+r
and no other bits
.RB ( 0644 / 0600
become
.BR 0640 ).
Mode and owner/group changes are logged
.RB ( chmod / chown ).
.IR state/
.RB ( 0700 ,
not served).
Removing the package does not delete
.IR users/
(operator files).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstash (8),
.BR bootstash (5),
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/QUICKSTART.md ,
.IR /usr/share/doc/bootstash/OPENVPN.md
